# ============================================================
# Flare_V2 — attributes. Root-only, same as .gitignore.
# Later rules win, so the byte-pinned artifacts come after the
# general `*` rule and override it.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Normal source ----------------
# Normalise to LF in the repo, check out native. Git's default with a modern
# core.autocrlf; stated so a misconfigured clone still gets consistent source.
*                        text=auto

# ---------------- Byte-pinned artifacts ----------------
# PLAN D21: the committed model weights and dataset partitions are verified
# byte-for-byte against sha256 digests recorded in metrics.json and
# CHECKSUMS.json. Those digests were computed on a Windows working tree, i.e.
# over CRLF bytes. Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true) normalises CRLF -> LF
# into the blob at commit time, so on any LF checkout — every ubuntu-latest CI
# runner — the files hash differently and every job that loads a model or runs
# `scripts.ci.run artifact_integrity` fails with a checksum mismatch.
#
# `-text` pins these paths to one byte representation: stored and checked out
# verbatim on every platform, no EOL translation, so the digest is stable.
# The .onnx and .npy already store verbatim (Git detected them binary); listing
# the whole trees here is harmless and documents the intent.
#
# Every tree here is consumed by a byte-exact hash somewhere:
#   backend/models/**            metrics.json / CHECKSUMS.json  (D21)
#   backend/data/splits/**       partition MANIFEST checksums_sha256
#   backend/app/rag/corpus/**    loader.corpus_hash() vs chunk_manifest.json
#                                (retriever refuses to load on a mismatch)
backend/models/**            -text
backend/data/splits/**       -text
backend/app/rag/corpus/**    -text
